  "description": "This extension is used on the DataRequirement structure, or any of its elements, to indicate that values for the data requirement could not be determined due to a processing exception. For example, the `code` element of a code filter may have an exception indicating the value could not be determined for function references.",
  "purpose": "Data requirements analysis (e.g. as performed by the $data-requirements operation) cannot always determine the values of every element of a data requirement. This extension allows the analysis to communicate that a value could not be determined, and why, so that consumers of the data requirements do not interpret the absence of a value as the absence of a requirement.",
  "fhirVersion": "4.0.1",
  "mapping": [
    {
      "identity": "rim",
      "uri": "http://hl7.org/v3",
      "name": "RIM Mapping"
    }
  ],
